You can also go through Gehennom with naught but a pick-axe for a weapon.
It goes faster with Grayswandir, though.

In the early game, you generally don't get to choose which artifact to use, so
the question of whether or not Grayswandir or Mojo is better is moot.
If your priest finds a Grayswandir in an early bones level, that's a better weapon than an expert mace (assuming you can survive the up-to-16 HP of blast
damage).

Anyway, don't be afraid to use artifact weapons where you're restricted.
This is especially true once you enchant them, and the price 60 scroll is easy
to identify.  In the early game, don't wait to bless the scroll; use it
uncursed on your artifact weapon.  

